          {
            "id": 440,
            "sort": 2,
            "name": "Overview",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-TiOVdSyheonG3IxARzClEfIbgqh\">Overall, while three countries witnessed rises in their proportions of self-employed workers during this period, the figures for Turkey and Greece showed declining trends. Additionally, despite experiencing the most significant drop, Turkey maintained the highest percentage throughout the period.</div>\n</div>",
            "question_id": 13797,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 441,
            "sort": 3,
            "name": "Body 1",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-P0pcdRkwxoNqnzx96YulIHESgmh\">Looking at countries with lower proportions, in 1998, the Russian Republic, Slovakia, and the Czech Republic all recorded figures of below 15%, standing at 5%, 7%, and 12%, respectively. The Czech Republic then saw its percentage increase to 15% in 2008, while similar upward trends were seen in Slovakia and the Russian Republic, with their figures rising to 12% and 7% respectively.</div>\n</div>",
            "question_id": 13797,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 442,
            "sort": 4,
            "name": "Body 2",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-LV3Sdhww4oopFSxiqD6l3lk4gPQ\">Regarding nations with higher proportions, Turkey led the group with about 55% of its workforce being self-employed in 1998, followed by Greece at just over 40%. However, both countries experienced decreases over the next decade, with Turkey's percentage falling to around 38% and Greece's dropping to about 35% by 2008.</div>\n</div>",
